<!-- GApps-only framework overlay (see lineage_Mi8937_gapps.mk). -->
<resources>
    <!-- Default on-device speech recognizer: the RecognitionService inside
         "Speech Recognition and Synthesis from Google" (com.google.android.tts,
         shipped by the NikGapps payload). Same value Pixel ships. With it:
           * Settings > System > Languages > Speech gains the AOSP "On-device
             recognition settings" row, which opens the app's declared
             settingsActivity (offline language-pack download screen). Without
             it that screen is unreachable from any menu, because AOSP's other
             route ("Voice input") is hidden whenever ro.config.low_ram=true
             drops the notLowRam android.software.voice_recognizers feature
             (GoTweaks low_ram toggle).
           * SpeechRecognizer.isOnDeviceRecognitionAvailable() becomes true,
             so apps can use the on-device (offline) recognizer.
         Must NOT be set on the vanilla product: the package does not exist
         there and Settings would log a missing-recognizer error. -->
    <string name="config_defaultOnDeviceSpeechRecognitionService" translatable="false">com.google.android.tts/com.google.android.apps.speech.tts.googletts.service.GoogleTTSRecognitionService</string>

    <!-- Default speech recognizer PACKAGE name (not a component; see
         VoiceInteractionManagerService.findAvailRecognizer(), which compares this
         value against ServiceInfo.packageName). Without it, the secure setting
         voice_recognition_service is never populated on pepito: findAvailRecognizer()'s
         fallback loop only accepts a recognizer carrying FLAG_SYSTEM, and nothing in
         the ROM (vanilla or gapps) ships a RecognitionService at all. The prefPackage
         match that runs ahead of that fallback has no system-app requirement, so
         naming the package here is what lets the Play-installed "Speech Recognition
         and Synthesis from Google" (com.google.android.tts, in /data/app) be picked
         as the default recognizer.

         Two things this deliberately does NOT do:
           * It does not grant the SYSTEM_SPEECH_RECOGNIZER role. That role is
             systemOnly="true" (PermissionController roles.xml) and
             Role.isPackageMinimallyQualifiedAsUser() rejects any package without
             FLAG_SYSTEM, so a /data-installed payload can never hold it. The role's
             RECORD_AUDIO and UPDATE_APP_OPS_STATS pregrants therefore do not happen.
           * It is not defeated by the GoTweaks low_ram toggle. mEnableService gates
             the voice *interactor* (assistant), not the recognizer; initRecognizer()
             runs unconditionally at the end of initForUserNoTracing().

         Must NOT be set on the vanilla product: the package does not exist there. -->
    <string name="config_systemSpeechRecognizer" translatable="false">com.google.android.tts</string>

    <!-- Pre-approve Android Auto's notification listener
         (com.google.android.gearhead.notifications.SharedNotificationListenerManager$ListenerService,
         declared by the AndroidAutoStubPrebuilt in /product/priv-app). Colon-separated package
         list; NotificationManagerService resolves each package's NotificationListenerService
         components at boot and, on FIRST boot only (no /data/system/notification_policy.xml
         yet, or a new user), writes them into enabled_notification_listeners. So this takes
         effect after a wipe/fresh flash, not a dirty flash; an existing unit still needs the
         one-time "Allow notification access" toggle (or
         `cmd notification allow_listener <component>`). The stub declares
         default_autobind_listenerservice=false, so approval alone does not keep the service
         bound; gearhead requests the bind itself when a head unit connects, exactly as after
         a manual grant. The Play-updated Android Auto keeps the same component name, so the
         approval survives the upgrade. Gapps-only: gearhead does not exist on vanilla. -->
    <string name="config_defaultListenerAccessPackages" translatable="false">com.google.android.projection.gearhead</string>
</resources>
